<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA-BOURSE CAPITALISATION MAINTAINS RISE.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA-BOURSE CAPITALISATION MAINTAINS RISE.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The total capitalisation of the</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse rose to 9.268 billion litas last week from 8.75</p>
<p>billion litas the previous week, the stock exchange said on</p>
<p>Monday.</p>
<p>The bourse also said that the capitalisation of the shares</p>
<p>quoted rose to 6.367 billion litas last week from 5.896 billion</p>
<p>litas the previous week.</p>
<p>It also said that the capitalisation of shares not quoted</p>
<p>on the bourse was 1.423 billion litas last week compared to</p>
<p>1.353 billion litas one week earlier.</p>
<p>The capitalisation of government T-bills was down to 1.478</p>
<p>billion litas last week from 1.502 billion litas the previous</p>
<p>week.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					 Aug 11 - 15     Aug 04-08</p>
<p>    Submitted orders	     16,071	    15,120</p>
<p>    Executed orders		1,886	     1,520</p>
<p>    Number of transactions on  1,388	     1,064</p>
<p>Central market (CM)</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL  6.158 mln	 38,311 mln</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)	    247		 224</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	61,010 mln	12.787 mln</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week   53.111 mln     52.614 mln</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week   6.984 mln	6.570 mln</p>
<p>Number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	  4		10</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	303,020	32.507 mln</p>
<p>-- Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
